# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SITE_URL — public base URL of the site (absolute, http/https, NO trailing slash).
# Single source of truth for canonicals, hreflang, Open Graph, JSON-LD and the
# sitemap. Centralized and validated in src/config/site.js.
#
# Set BOTH variables to the same value:
#   - VITE_SITE_URL → exposed to the app/SSG bundle by Vite (browser + prerender).
#   - SITE_URL      → read by Node build scripts that run outside Vite (sitemap, etc.).
#
# Per environment:
#   - Local dev / local build : if unset, falls back to http://localhost:5173.
#   - Deployed build (Vercel/CI): a real domain is REQUIRED. If VITE_SITE_URL is not
#     set, the production build FAILS with a clear error instead of emitting
#     localhost canonicals. The vercel.app domain is never used automatically.
#
# Format rules (enforced in src/config/site.js):
#   - Must be an absolute URL using http: or https:.
#   - No embedded credentials (no user:pass@host).
#   - Trailing slashes are stripped automatically.
#   - https is recommended in production; http is intended only for localhost.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
